      "summary": {
        "headline": "Periodicals mail volume and per-household receipt have declined significantly over the long term, with projections indicating continued decreases.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Periodicals per household decreased by 49.4% from 43.3 pieces per household per year in FY2014 to 21.9 pieces per household per year in FY2025. It also decreased by 45.2% over the last 10 years (from 40.0 pieces in FY2015 to 21.9 pieces in FY2025) and by 26.0% over the last 5 years (from 29.6 pieces in FY2020 to 21.9 pieces in FY2025).",
            "metric": "periodicals-per-household",
            "years": [
              2014,
              2025,
              2015,
              2020
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "However, Periodicals per household increased by 2.0 pieces, or 10.1%, from 19.9 pieces per household per year in FY2024 to 21.9 pieces per household per year in FY2025.",
            "metric": "periodicals-per-household",
            "years": [
              2024,
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Periodicals received by households decreased by 50.0% from 6800.0 millions of pieces in FY2003 to 3400.0 millions of pieces in FY2023. It also decreased by 40.4% over the last 10 years (from 5700.0 millions of pieces in FY2013 to 3400.0 millions of pieces in FY2023) and by 22.7% over the last 5 years (from 4400.0 millions of pieces in FY2018 to 3400.0 millions of pieces in FY2023).",
            "metric": "periodicals-volume",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2013,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Periodicals received by households increased by 100.0 millions of pieces, or 3.0%, from 3300.0 millions of pieces in FY2022 to 3400.0 millions of pieces in FY2023.",
            "metric": "periodicals-volume",
            "years": [
              2022,
              2023
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A linear trend projection for Periodicals received by households, which beats the naive baseline, forecasts a decline from 2995.0 millions of pieces in FY2024 to 2023.0 millions of pieces in FY2028. The 80% confidence interval for FY2024 is 2782.0 to 3209.0 millions of pieces, and for FY2028 it is 1546.0 to 2500.0 millions of pieces.",
            "metric": "periodicals-volume",
            "years": [
              2024,
              2028
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Comparisons for Periodicals per household and Periodicals received by households across FY2010 should be cautious due to a restatement of diary data with new weighting methodology.",
          "Comparisons for Periodicals per household and Periodicals received by households across FY2012 should be cautious because FY2014 data restated 2012 and 2013 values due to weighting by home ownership.",
